# Bitwarden files that Multiwarden does not carry or replaces with its own: Bitwarden's
# developer tooling, repository automation (code owners, labels, review and response bots)
# and its issue and pull request templates. The upstream sync leaves changes to these paths
# out, so removed files stay removed and Multiwarden's own versions are kept.
# Entries are git pathspecs: [x] matches the letter x (used for the AI assistant configuration
# folder) and a trailing /* matches everything under a folder.
.[c]laude/*
.mcp.json
.github/CODEOWNERS
.github/label-pr.json
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
# Bitwarden's GitHub Actions workflows need Bitwarden's secrets and infrastructure, so none of
# them are carried, and new ones Bitwarden adds stay out. Multiwarden's own workflows
# (multiwarden-*.yml) are not in upstream, so they are unaffected.
.github/workflows/*
